Title:
BOF, Crystal Palace Linker and The JellyBee System KORE Compiler

Type:
Blog Post

Short Summary (4-8 sentences max):
- This post analyzes modern red team “system” architectures where implants are kept minimal and capabilities are compiled, stored, transformed, and loaded on-demand to reduce operational footprint under EDR/SIEM visibility.  
- It explains how EDR telemetry is built from supported Windows contracts (process/image callbacks, Ob callbacks, minifilters, WFP, ETW) and why modular execution doesn’t remove telemetry but can reduce persistent implant complexity.  
- The author breaks down Beacon Object Files (BOFs) as COFF objects executed by Cobalt Strike Beacon acting as a mini COFF linker/loader, including COFF relocations and DFR (MODULE$Function) import resolution.  
- It then covers Raphael Mudge’s Crystal Palace linker approach to produce position-independent “PICO/PIC” artifacts from BOFs via linker scripts, enabling execution without a full Beacon by embedding a runner/loader and resolving imports via provided interfaces.  
- Finally, it introduces the JellyBeeKORE (JBKORE) compiler concept: generating PIC/shellcode directly at codegen time (not post-COFF), controlling fixups, ABI setup, API resolution via PEB/EAT (including forwarders and API sets), and optional unwind metadata registration.  
- Useful for red team operators, toolchain developers, and malware researchers building modular post-exploitation chains that can move across processes while minimizing static dependencies.

Technical Focus:
- Windows EDR telemetry sources (PsSetCreateProcessNotifyRoutineEx, PsSetLoadImageNotifyRoutine, ObRegisterCallbacks, ETW, WFP, minifilters)
- COFF/BOF internals: symbols, IMAGE_RELOCATION, AMD64 relocation types, DFR import model
- Linker/loader mechanics: resolving relocations, building PIC/PICO, embedding loaders/runners
- Crystal Palace .spec scripting: merge/mergelib, attach/redirect, DFR resolvers (hash/string), bss/unwind handling
- PIC compiler design (JBKORE): fixups at codegen, Win64 ABI/shadow space, PEB/Ldr export resolution, API set/forwarders
- x64 exception/unwind support for generated code (RtlAddFunctionTable / RtlInstallFunctionTableCallback)

Use Cases:
- Build modular post-exploitation capabilities that load only when needed (reduced implant bloat)
- Execute BOF-like modules without full Beacon by generating PIC + embedded runner
- Create custom in-memory toolchains (compile/link/transform) for segmented or offline environments
- Implement custom API resolvers (PEB/EAT, hashing, API set mapping) for shellcode/PIC payloads
- Experiment with linker-time transformations (function reordering, mutation, dead-code removal) to vary artifacts

Keywords:
EDR telemetry, ETW, WFP, minifilter, ObRegisterCallbacks, PsSetCreateProcessNotifyRoutineEx, PsSetLoadImageNotifyRoutine, PatchGuard, Cobalt Strike, Beacon Object File, BOF, COFF, IMAGE_RELOCATION, IMAGE_REL_AMD64_REL32, DFR, Crystal Palace linker, PICO, PIC, PEB, PEB_LDR_DATA, IMAGE_EXPORT_DIRECTORY, API Set, forwarder exports, Win64 ABI, shadow space, RtlAddFunctionTable